, +, -, *, /, parentheses) with correct precedence. The solution must use the generated parser for evaluation rather than manual token processing.\n\nTASK_TRACKING:\n1. \u23f3 Create project structure and .fsproj file - COMPLETED (Created Calculator.fsproj with FsLexYacc 11.3.0 reference and build targets)\n2. \u23f3 Create Lexer.fsl (FsLex specification) - IN_PROGRESS (Fixed token references to use `Parser` module; currently failing build due to lexer syntax error on line 22)\n3. \u23f3 Create Parser.fsy (FsYacc specification) - COMPLETED (Defined tokens, precedence, and grammar rules)\n4. \u23f3 Create Program.fs (Entry point) - COMPLETED (Implemented main function to parse and print result)\n5. \u23f3 Fix Build Configuration - IN_PROGRESS (Switched from manual `dotnet fslex` to MSBuild integration via FsLexYacc.targets; investigating lexer file formatting issue)\n\nCOMPLETED:\n- Project structure created with FsLexYacc 11.3.0 dependencies.\n- Parser grammar defined with correct precedence (PLUS/MINUS, TIMES/DIVIDE, UMINUS).\n- Program entry point implemented to accept command-line arguments.\n- Identified that FsLexYacc 11.x uses MSBuild targets (`FsLex`/`FsYacc` item types) rather than global tools.\n\nPENDING:\n- Resolve Lexer.fsl syntax error (Unexpected character '}' on line 22).\n- Verify generated Lexer.fs and Parser.fs are correct.\n- Test the calculator with various expressions.\n\nCURRENT_STATE:\n- Directory: /Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-b/fsharp-r2\n- Files: Calculator.fsproj, Lexer.fsl, Parser.fsy, Program.fs\n- Build Status: Failing. Error: `Lexer.fsl(22): error : Unexpected character '}'`.\n- Investigation: The lexer file header uses `open Parser`. The error suggests a formatting issue with the closing brace `}` of the header block or trailing content on that line. Hex dump shows the file ends with `} }` or similar, but the error points to line 22. The lexer rules reference `Parser.INTEGER`, `Parser.PLUS`, etc., which aligns with the generated parser module name.\n\nCODE_STATE:\n- Calculator.fsproj: Uses `<ItemGroup><FsLex Include=\"Lexer.fsl\" /></ItemGroup>` and `<ItemGroup><FsYacc Include=\"Parser.fsy\" /></ItemGroup>` for MSBuild integration.\n- Lexer.fsl:\n  ```fsharp\n  {\n  module Lexer\n\n  open System\n  open Parser\n  }\n\n  let whitespace = [' ' '\\t' '\\r' '\\n']\n  let digit = ['0'-'9']\n\n  rule tokenize = parse\n    | whitespace+    { tokenize lexbuf }\n    | digit+         { int_of_string (lexeme lexbuf) |> Parser.INTEGER }\n    | '+'            { Parser.PLUS }\n    | '-'            { Parser.MINUS }\n    | '*'            { Parser.TIMES }\n    | '/'            { Parser.DIVIDE }\n    | '('            { Parser.LPAREN }\n    | ')'            { Parser.RPAREN }\n    | eof            { Parser.EOF }\n    | _              { invalid_arg (sprintf \"Unexpected character: %s\" (lexeme_string lexbuf)) }\n  ```\n- Parser.fsy:\n  ```fsharp\n  %{\n  module Parser\n  %}\n\n  %token <int> INTEGER\n  %token PLUS\n  %token MINUS\n  %token TIMES\n  %token DIVIDE\n  %token LPAREN\n  %token RPAREN\n  %token EOF\n\n  %left PLUS MINUS\n  %left TIMES DIVIDE\n  %nonassoc UMINUS\n\n  %start <int> expression\n  %type <int> expression\n\n  %%\n\n  expression:\n    | expr = expr; EOF { expr }\n\n  expr:\n    | LEFT = expr; op = TIMES; RIGHT = expr { LEFT * RIGHT }\n    | LEFT = expr; op = DIVIDE; RIGHT = expr { LEFT / RIGHT }\n    | LEFT = expr; op = PLUS; RIGHT = expr { LEFT + RIGHT }\n    | LEFT = expr; op = MINUS; RIGHT = expr { LEFT - RIGHT }\n    | n = INTEGER { n }\n    | LPAREN; e = expr; RPAREN { e }\n  ```\n- Program.fs:\n  ```fsharp\n  open System\n  open System.IO\n  open Lexer\n  open Parser\n\n  [<EntryPoint>]\n  let main argv =\n      if argv.Length <> 1 then\n          printfn \"Usage: Calculator <expression>\"\n          1\n      else\n          try\n              let expression = argv.[0]\n              let lexbuf = LexBuffer<char>.FromTextReader(new StringReader(expression))\n              let result = parse tokenize lexbuf\n              printfn \"%d\" result\n              0\n          with e ->\n              printfn \"Error: %s\" e.Message\n              1\n  ```\n\nTESTS:\n- Build Error: `Lexer.fsl(22): error : Unexpected character '}'`\n- Build Error: `MSB3073: The command \"dotnet ... fslex.dll\" ... exited with code 1`\n\nCHANGES:\n- Updated Calculator.fsproj to use FsLex/FsYacc item types instead of manual build targets.\n- Updated Lexer.fsl to reference `Parser` module for tokens instead of `Tok`.\n- Attempted to fix Lexer.fsl formatting issues via terminal echo and hex dump analysis.\n\nDEPS:\n- FsLexYacc 11.3.0 (NuGet)\n- .NET SDK 10.0.203\n\nVERSION_CONTROL_STATUS:\n- No git operations recorded in recent events.", "summary_offset": 4, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-1452c6b2-a9f2-4eab-b9cd-7e700b3a4446", "kind": "Condensation"}
