, +, -, *, /, parentheses) with correct precedence. The solution must use the generated parser for evaluation rather than manual token processing.\n\nTASK_TRACKING:\n1. \u23f3 Create project structure and .fsproj file - COMPLETED (Created Calculator.fsproj with FsLexYacc 11.3.0 reference and build targets)\n2. \u23f3 Create Lexer.fsl (FsLex specification) - IN_PROGRESS (Blocked by FsLex parsing error: \"Unexpected character '}'\" on line 22. Investigating FsLex syntax rules regarding brace nesting in action code blocks.)\n\nCOMPLETED:\n- Project structure created.\n- Identified that FsLex is failing to parse the `Lexer.fsl` file specifically at the closing brace of the rule block.\n- Investigated FsLexYacc source code to understand how it parses `.fsl` files (looking at `fslexlex.fsl` and `fslexpars.fsy`).\n\nPENDING:\n- Fix `Lexer.fsl` syntax to resolve the \"Unexpected character '}'\" error.\n- Generate `Lexer.fs` from `Lexer.fsl`.\n- Create `Parser.fsy` and `Parser.fs`.\n- Implement evaluation logic.\n\nCURRENT_STATE:\n- Working Directory: `/Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-b/fsharp-r2`\n- Error: `Lexer.fsl(22,0): error: Unexpected character '}'`\n- The error occurs when FsLex tries to parse the closing `}` of the `rule tokenize` block.\n- The agent suspects the issue is related to how FsLex distinguishes between F# code braces `{ }` inside the rule actions and the lexer's structural braces.\n- The agent is currently examining the FsLexYacc source code (`fslexlex.fs`, `fslexpars.fsy`) to understand the expected format of the `.fsl` file, specifically how code blocks are delimited.\n\nCODE_STATE:\n- File: `Lexer.fsl`\n- Content Snippet:\n  ```fsharp\n  open System\n  open Parser\n  }\n\n  let whitespace = [' ' '\\t' '\\r' '\\n']\n  let digit = ['0'-'9']\n\n  rule tokenize = parse\n    | whitespace+    { tokenize lexbuf }\n    | digit+         { int_of_string (lexeme lexbuf) |> Parser.INTEGER }\n    | '+'            { Parser.PLUS }\n    | '-'            { Parser.MINUS }\n    | '*'            { Parser.TIMES }\n    | '/'            { Parser.DIVIDE }\n    | '('            { Parser.LPAREN }\n    | ')'            { Parser.RPAREN }\n    | eof            { Parser.EOF }\n    | _              { failwith (sprintf \"Unexpected character: %s\" (lexeme_string lexbuf)) }\n  }\n  ```\n- Note: The header ends with `}`. The rule block ends with `}`. The error is on the final `}`.\n\nTESTS:\n- Build fails with exit code 1 due to FsLex parsing error.\n\nCHANGES:\n- Attempted to simplify error handling from `invalid_arg` to `failwith` to rule out library-specific syntax issues, but error persists.\n\nDEPS:\n- FsLexYacc 11.3.0\n\nVERSION_CONTROL_STATUS:\n- No commits recorded in this session yet.", "summary_offset": 4, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-677fceb2-1c2d-4a4d-893b-2db0b1f84d80", "kind": "Condensation"}
